From d69a89cf91809e58cf7ccf5db61d865d2dbf1242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:56:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/33] prefill mmq tab: STRATA_MMQ_TAB off by default, the
 nine tested types only, not on gfx906

Review fixes for the pointer-table MMQ build:
- STRATA_MMQ_TAB defaults to OFF, like STRATA_MMQ_KQUANTS: the engine loads every kernel at start
  (CUDA_MODULE_LOADING=EAGER), and the nine tab instances took 36-38 MiB of VRAM per GPU (sm_86, measured with
  a cudaMemGetInfo probe linked with and without the tab objects; equal under LAZY), with STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT unset
  too. prep_group_kernel is compiled only with STRATA_MMQ_TAB, so a build without it has the same device code as
  3adce85 (the 58 cubins and PTX of build/strata are byte-identical to engine/strata-g3b's).
- The fingerprint block and the tab TUs are skipped on STRATA_HIP_GFX906: that build compiles no .cu from here, so
  the define, the uncompiled TUs and an unlinkable prefill_mmq_tab_test no longer appear.
- Tab instances only for Q2_0 IQ2_XXS IQ2_XS IQ2_S IQ3_XXS IQ3_S IQ4_NL IQ4_XS Q8_0, the types prefill_mmq_tab_test
  checks bit for bit; Q5_0 and the K-quants (STRATA_ORCA_Q4KS_MMQ, STRATA_MMQ_KQUANTS) keep the gather.
- overread_bytes takes the largest over-read of any config, not the over-read of the largest K tile (the over-read
  is not monotonic in the tile length).
- The test fails (instead of skipping) when a tested type has no tab, checks that Q5_0/K-quants report none, and
  pins the sm_86 over-reads (0, 72, 136 B); the dead K-quant scale branch is gone.
- SYCL's moe_mmq.dp.cpp gets the STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT stubs (false/0), for a future migrated prefill.cpp.
- moe_mmq.hpp points at docs/DETAILS.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
